//==============
// [Ref-1]
//==============
// Kill All Monsters: 0 / 1 - Need to Kill ALL Monster before go to next Stage (If time limit is reached, event will fail)

//==============
// [Ref-2]
//==============
// Party Enter: 0 - NO Party Enter / 1 - Will move all Party members in 10 Cords arround who Talk to NPC (All Need Tickets) / 2: Same as 1 but only need 1 Ticket (Who talk to NPC)

0
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Event Settings
// Switch and basic rules of the event.
//   Every monster must die: A monster stage only ends when all its monsters are dead; if time runs out first, the event fails.
//   Players needed: Players needed to start; with fewer the event is cancelled.
//   Players allowed: Most players that can enter (up to 30).
//   Needs an entry item: 1 takes the entry item (second part below) from each player who enters.
//   Only master characters: 1 lets in only characters at their third evolution or higher.
//   PKs can enter: 1 lets players with a PK level (murderers) in; 0 keeps them out.
//   Party entry: 0 Only the player who asks | 1 Whole party, each member needs a ticket | 2 Whole party, only the one who asks needs a ticket
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~1]      [Number]           [1~30]        [1~30]        [0~1]          [0~1]          [0~1]           [Number]
//  Enabled    KillAllMonsters    MinPlayers    MaxPlayers    RequireItem    OnlyMasters    AllowPKEnter    PartyEnter
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1          1                  1             20            1              0              1               2
end

1
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Timers
// Waiting times.
//   Wait before it starts (seconds): Seconds the players wait inside before the first stage starts.
//   Wait before players are moved out (seconds): Seconds after the event ends before the players are moved out.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~99999]    [0~99999]
//  StartTime    EndTime
//----------------------------------------------------------
    30           30
end

2
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Who Can Enter
// What a player needs to enter. * in a limit means no limit.
//   Entry item: Item category of the entry item.
//   Entry item index: Item index of the entry item.
//   Item level: Level the entry item must have. * accepts any level.
//   How many: How many of the entry item are taken from each player.
//   Level, at least: The lowest level that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Level, at most: The highest level that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Resets, at least: The fewest resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Resets, at most: The most resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Master resets, at least: The fewest master resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Master resets, at most: The most master resets that can enter. * has no limit.
//   Account level: -1 Every account level | 0 Free | 1 VIP 1 | 2 VIP 2 | 3 VIP 3
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~15]         [0~511]      [*/0~15]     [0~9999]     [*/0~15000]    [*/1~15000]    [*/0~999999]    [*/0~999999]    [*/0~999999]      [*/0~999999]      [0~3]
//  ItemSection    ItemIndex    ItemLevel    ItemCount    MinLevel       MaxLevel       MinReset        MaxReset        MinMasterReset    MaxMasterReset    AccountLevel
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    12             15           0            1            0              400            0               10000           0                 999               -1
end

3
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Schedule
// When the event starts. The seconds do not exist here: it starts on the minute.
//   Year: The year when the event starts. * means every year.
//   Month: The month when the event starts. * means every month.
//   Day: The day of the month when the event starts. * means every day of the month.
//   Day of the week: -1 Every day | 1 Sunday | 2 Monday | 3 Tuesday | 4 Wednesday | 5 Thursday | 6 Friday | 7 Saturday
//   Hour: The hour when the event starts. * means every hour.
//   Minute: The minute when the event starts. * means every minute.
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [*/1970~9999]    [*/1~12]    [*/1~31]    [*/1~7]      [*/0~23]    [*/0~59]
//  Year             Month       Day         DayOfWeek    Hour        Minute
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    *                *           *           *            10          46
end

//==============
// [Ref-3]
//==============
// Type: 0: Normal (Need to Kill Monsters taking settings of time and etc...) / 1: PvP Only (No Monsters Check no matter Settings - Monsters will be addade anyway if you set bellow)

4
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Stages
// The stages, in the order of the file. Each lasts its minutes; the next one starts when the time ends (or, in a monster stage that needs every monster dead, when they are all dead).
//   Stage: Number of the stage. The monsters and the points use it.
//   Lasts (minutes): Minutes the stage lasts.
//   Kind: 0 Monsters | 1 PvP only | 2 PvP, back to the start
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~300]    [0~9999]    [Number]
//  Stage      Minutes     StageType
//----------------------------------------------------------
    0          2           0
    1          2           0
    2          2           0
    3          2           0
    4          2           0
    5          2           0
    6          2           0
    6          2           0
    7          2           0
    8          2           0
    9          2           0
    10         2           0
    11         2           0
    12         2           0
    13         2           0
    14         2           0
    15         2           0
end

